<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">HMT Empire Windrush</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">HMT Empire Windrush was a passenger ship, built in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in 1930 as the Monte Rosa, that brought more than a thousand passengers, most of them from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, to Tilbury in June 1948. Its arrival became a symbol of post-war Commonwealth migration to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, and the migrants of that era are known as the Windrush generation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hmt-empire-windrush.jpg" alt="HMT Empire Windrush" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Royal Navy official photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HMT_Empire_Windrush_FL9448.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
